{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"6399fe554f519f37","type":"group","x":720,"y":2320,"width":556,"height":257,"label":"Commands"},
		{"id":"8a52c16451ee1242","type":"group","x":3543,"y":5720,"width":337,"height":356,"label":"Commands"},
		{"id":"a6c09a1c305c04e0","type":"text","text":"# Enumeration","x":-453,"y":-120,"width":177,"height":60},
		{"id":"26d2940ec20e8500","type":"text","text":"#### What is enumeration\nEnumeration = Active information gathering \nExtracts detailed data about a system \nUsally follows the scanning phase","x":-160,"y":-159,"width":356,"height":139},
		{"id":"d22dd9ec082745f9","type":"text","text":"Helps identify system weaknesses\nGather info like : \n- username, group name, network resourse, system banner\n\nUsed by both attacker and pentester","x":-134,"y":80,"width":304,"height":187},
		{"id":"a3f99248782a08b0","type":"text","text":"NetBIOS","x":429,"y":-120,"width":94,"height":60},
		{"id":"ff44caa7798ca8fc","type":"text","text":"NetBIOS ek network communication protocol/API hai jo local network (LAN) me computers ko ek dusre ko identify (naam se pehchanne), communicate karne aur files/printers share karne me help karta hai.","x":660,"y":-147,"width":425,"height":115},
		{"id":"69df4b78989624e7","type":"text","text":"| Service                         | Port    | Kaam                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **NetBIOS Name Service (NBNS)** | UDP 137 | Computer name ko IP address me resolve karta hai.       |\n| **NetBIOS Datagram Service**    | UDP 138 | Connectionless messages bhejta hai.                     |\n| **NetBIOS Session Service**     | TCP 139 | File aur printer sharing ke liye connection banata hai. |\n","x":499,"y":-360,"width":747,"height":134},
		{"id":"47f3c1b44bde3187","type":"text","text":"Attacker NetBIOS ka use information collect (enumeration) karne ke liye karta hai.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Computer Name\n- Username\n- Workgroup/Domain\n- Shared Folders\n- Logged-in User\n- MAC Address","x":499,"y":-700,"width":358,"height":296},
		{"id":"f0c68beac3d44635","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sU -p 137 <IP>`","x":873,"y":-464,"width":193,"height":60},
		{"id":"5c94ddd937b0bb23","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script nbstat.nse -p137 <IP>`","x":873,"y":-532,"width":313,"height":60},
		{"id":"2a9c228e2741b60a","type":"text","text":"`nbtscan <IP>`","x":873,"y":-612,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1414e9969a0d38d5","type":"text","text":"`enum4linux <IP>`","x":873,"y":-692,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f1e2f79e0c71cfdd","type":"text","text":"| NetBIOS                          | DNS                                   |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| LAN ke liye bana tha             | Internet aur LAN dono me use hota hai |\n| Computer names resolve karta hai | Domain names resolve karta hai        |\n| UDP 137                          | UDP/TCP 53                            |\n| Legacy Windows networks          | Modern networks                       |\n","x":499,"y":-900,"width":590,"height":169},
		{"id":"02df34fe9879c9dc","type":"text","text":"NetBIOS = Network Basic Input/Output System\nPurpose: LAN me computers ko naam se identify aur communicate karna.\nUDP 137: Name Service (NBNS)\nUDP 138: Datagram Service\nTCP 139: Session Service (SMB over NetBIOS)\nUse: File sharing, printer sharing, name resolution.\nCybersecurity: Enumeration ke liye computer name, users, shares, workgroup/domain jaise details nikalne me kaam aata hai.","x":499,"y":-1140,"width":590,"height":226},
		{"id":"49ee4919c39cdfe0","type":"text","text":"Attacker can use NetBIOS enumeration to gather information about a target network, like the machine name, IP address, user name and more","x":1140,"y":-135,"width":395,"height":92},
		{"id":"40a4783db7ef848d","type":"text","text":"SNMP","x":429,"y":114,"width":77,"height":60},
		{"id":"5ca9c04dd7ab0254","type":"text","text":"SNMP ek network management protocol hai jiska use network devices (router, switch, firewall, printer, server, IoT devices) ko monitor aur manage karne ke liye hota hai.","x":660,"y":90,"width":360,"height":109},
		{"id":"87eb2888ed78fcbb","type":"text","text":"SNMP administrators ko network devices ki information dekhne aur kuch settings manage karne ki facility deta hai.","x":660,"y":240,"width":360,"height":100},
		{"id":"143f66e46b2338f2","type":"text","text":"Maan lo company me 100 routers hain.\nAdministrator har router me login nahi karega.\nWo SNMP ki help se ek hi jagah se dekh sakta hai:\n\nRouter ON hai ya OFF\nCPU Usage\nRAM Usage\nNetwork Traffic\nTemperature\nInterface Status\nUptime","x":1160,"y":80,"width":406,"height":290},
		{"id":"463c16f3b7db2d3b","type":"text","text":"                 SNMP Manager\n            (Monitoring Server)\n                    |\n        -------------------------\n        |          |           |\n        |          |           |\n      SNMP       SNMP        SNMP\n      Agent      Agent       Agent\n        |          |           |\n     Router     Switch      Printer","x":1620,"y":72,"width":324,"height":306},
		{"id":"8b81f09a291f4569","type":"text","text":"SNMP Manager → Information collect karta hai.\nSNMP Agent → Device ke andar chalne wali service jo information provide karti hai.","x":2040,"y":72,"width":655,"height":55},
		{"id":"56377724e1deb96c","type":"text","text":"| Component                             | Kaam                                       |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Manager**                           | Information request karta hai.             |\n| **Agent**                             | Device se data bhejta hai.                 |\n| **MIB (Management Information Base)** | Device ki information ka database.         |\n| **OID (Object Identifier)**           | MIB ke andar har information ka unique ID. |\n","x":2040,"y":141,"width":637,"height":169},
		{"id":"35c3aebcec1cec34","type":"text","text":"| Protocol  | Port    |\n| --------- | ------- |\n| SNMP      | UDP 161 |\n| SNMP Trap | UDP 162 |\n","x":2040,"y":328,"width":211,"height":100},
		{"id":"8fe644a31b021f7e","type":"text","text":"Example:\n\nHostname\nOS\nNetwork Interfaces\nIP Address\nMAC Address\nRunning Processes (kuch devices)\nInstalled Software\nUptime\nRouting Table\nNetwork Statistics","x":323,"y":213,"width":289,"height":314},
		{"id":"eead603a751e6fa4","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sU -p161 <IP>`","x":660,"y":360,"width":185,"height":60},
		{"id":"e8a49ec212feae09","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script snmp-info -sU -p161 <IP>`","x":660,"y":440,"width":335,"height":60},
		{"id":"f318c571b596e06b","type":"text","text":"`snmpwalk -v2c -c public <IP>`","x":867,"y":360,"width":256,"height":60},
		{"id":"9d5a4f76294e0eed","type":"text","text":"`snmpwalk -v2c -c public 192.168.1.10`","x":1020,"y":440,"width":319,"height":60},
		{"id":"27c152d4a5b79600","type":"text","text":"`onesixtyone -c community.txt <IP>`","x":1160,"y":380,"width":296,"height":50},
		{"id":"e6f313e42d37c16c","type":"text","text":"| Point                     | Answer                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Full Form                 | Simple Network Management Protocol                                                                       |\n| Purpose                   | Network devices ko monitor aur manage karna                                                              |\n| Port                      | UDP 161                                                                                                  |\n| Trap Port                 | UDP 162                                                                                                  |\n| Manager                   | Requests bhejta hai                                                                                      |\n| Agent                     | Information provide karta hai                                                                            |\n| MIB                       | Device information database                                                                              |\n| OID                       | MIB object ka unique identifier                                                                          |\n| Versions                  | v1, v2c, v3                                                                                              |\n| Default Community Strings | `public`, `private`                                                                                      |\n| Enumeration Tool          | `snmpwalk`, `onesixtyone`, `nmap --script snmp-info`                                                     |\n| Risk                      | Agar community string weak/default ho, to attacker sensitive device information enumerate kar sakta hai. |\n","x":2760,"y":29,"width":1020,"height":393},
		{"id":"b1c30a0366e61539","type":"text","text":"# SMB","x":323,"y":920,"width":85,"height":60},
		{"id":"e6f328ecb5e689b9","type":"text","text":"SMB (Server Message Block) ek network file-sharing protocol hai jiska use files, folders, printers aur network resources ko share karne ke liye hota hai.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nSMB ki help se ek computer dusre computer ki shared files ya printers access kar sakta hai.","x":525,"y":858,"width":598,"height":185},
		{"id":"80c24a6cc026588b","type":"text","text":"SMB Ka Kaam\n✅ File Sharing\n✅ Folder Sharing\n✅ Printer Sharing\n✅ Remote File Access\n✅ Windows Network Communication","x":1200,"y":863,"width":314,"height":175},
		{"id":"be8c21effd756f12","type":"text","text":"| Version | Status                          |\n| ------- | ------------------------------- |\n| SMBv1   | ❌ Old, insecure                 |\n| SMBv2   | ✅ Faster                        |\n| SMBv3   | ✅ Secure (Encryption supported) |\n","x":1357,"y":560,"width":369,"height":134},
		{"id":"9a4d8d59b4a27e4d","type":"text","text":"| Port    | Purpose                |\n| ------- | ---------------------- |\n| TCP 139 | SMB over NetBIOS (Old) |\n| TCP 445 | Direct SMB (Modern)    |\n","x":997,"y":560,"width":304,"height":134},
		{"id":"87c1546951655621","type":"text","text":"SMB URL Example\n```\n\\\\192.168.1.10\\Public\n```\n\n```\n\\\\SERVER\\Documents\n```","x":1580,"y":850,"width":245,"height":202},
		{"id":"da0b0f009dfec657","type":"text","text":"Agar TCP 445 open ho, attacker ye information nikal sakta hai:\n\nComputer Name\nHostname\nDomain Name\nShared Folders\nUsers\nOS Version\nSMB Version\nPermissions","x":525,"y":1060,"width":272,"height":340},
		{"id":"1e9288873e269780","type":"text","text":"`nmap -p445 <IP>`","x":824,"y":1060,"width":153,"height":60},
		{"id":"b4e35d7c95738a4c","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sV -p445 <IP>`","x":824,"y":1145,"width":185,"height":60},
		{"id":"e58e35699e7beade","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script smb-enum-shares,smb-enum-users -p445 <IP>`","x":1009,"y":1060,"width":470,"height":60},
		{"id":"8ce27fb52df9db92","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script smb-os-discovery -p445 <IP>`","x":1040,"y":1145,"width":359,"height":60},
		{"id":"65da7ab2f1c2872d","type":"text","text":"`smbclient -L //<IP> -N`","x":824,"y":1220,"width":209,"height":60},
		{"id":"ba297e4ca65c11ec","type":"text","text":"`enum4linux <IP>`","x":1047,"y":1220,"width":153,"height":60},
		{"id":"308a019032a3a4a6","type":"text","text":"`netexec smb $IP`\n\nYe SMB version, hostname, domain aur authentication status jaise details dikhata hai.","x":820,"y":1293,"width":600,"height":107},
		{"id":"ec24d74ea7334e97","type":"text","text":"Ye enumerate kar sakta hai:\n\nUsers\nShares\nGroups\nDomain\nPassword Policy","x":1440,"y":1153,"width":238,"height":194},
		{"id":"aec72a92c3a30128","type":"text","text":"| SMB                     | NetBIOS                                  |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| File sharing protocol   | Name resolution & session service        |\n| Modern Windows networks | Legacy Windows networking                |\n| TCP 445                 | UDP 137, UDP 138, TCP 139                |\n| Direct communication    | SMB ko support kar sakta hai (old setup) |\n","x":1880,"y":850,"width":551,"height":169},
		{"id":"5709334f24829bc9","type":"text","text":"| Point              | Answer                                       |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Full Form          | Server Message Block                         |\n| Purpose            | File, folder, printer sharing                |\n| Modern Port        | TCP 445                                      |\n| Old Port           | TCP 139 (over NetBIOS)                       |\n| Insecure Version   | SMBv1                                        |\n| Secure Versions    | SMBv2, SMBv3                                 |\n| Enumeration Tools  | `smbclient`, `enum4linux`, `netexec`, `nmap` |\n| Common Information | Shares, users, hostname, domain, SMB version |\n","x":1880,"y":1038,"width":565,"height":283},
		{"id":"27aa2140ed2bf8a9","type":"text","text":"### Active Directory","x":380,"y":1760,"width":189,"height":60},
		{"id":"ef0cded65f7ebc69","type":"text","text":"Active Directory (AD) Microsoft ki directory service hai jo company ke users, computers, groups aur permissions ko centrally manage karti hai.\n\nSimple words me:\n\nActive Directory ek database hai jisme company ke sabhi users, computers aur groups ki information aur unki permissions store hoti hain.","x":680,"y":1698,"width":593,"height":185},
		{"id":"2b39db9dc88eaf9a","type":"text","text":"Ek company me 500 employees hain.\nAdmin ko har computer par alag user banana nahi padta.\nWo Active Directory me ek baar user create karta hai.\n\nUsername : akash\nPassword : ***\nDepartment : IT\n\nAb Akash kisi bhi company PC me login kar sakta hai.","x":1400,"y":1674,"width":623,"height":234},
		{"id":"bc7b8982ce6b88cb","type":"text","text":"                 Domain Controller\n              (Active Directory)\n                      |\n      ----------------------------------\n      |               |               |\n    User1          User2         User3\n     Akash         Rahul         Neha\n      |               |              |\n    Laptop         Desktop       Printer","x":1780,"y":1360,"width":363,"height":273},
		{"id":"c919dc45a94c7dfd","type":"text","text":"##### AD Objects\nActive Directory me bahut objects hote hain.\n\n- Users\n- Groups\n- Computers\n- Printers\n- Organizational Units (OU)\n- Domains","x":713,"y":1989,"width":363,"height":274},
		{"id":"18d6d85289629563","type":"text","text":"| Group                | Purpose                             |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Domain Admins        | Sabse powerful administrators       |\n| Enterprise Admins    | Multiple domains manage karte hain  |\n| Domain Users         | Normal users                        |\n| Domain Computers     | Domain ke computers                 |\n| Administrators       | Local/Domain administrators         |\n| Backup Operators     | Backup aur restore                  |\n| Account Operators    | User accounts manage kar sakte hain |\n| Remote Desktop Users | Remote Desktop login allowed        |\n","x":1180,"y":1985,"width":497,"height":283},
		{"id":"b6f1d79860ebaaee","type":"text","text":"| Point              | Answer                                                     |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Active Directory   | Microsoft ki directory service                             |\n| User               | Individual account                                         |\n| Group              | Multiple users ka collection                               |\n| Domain Users       | Default user group                                         |\n| Domain Admins      | Highest privilege group                                    |\n| Domain Controller  | AD server jo users aur policies manage karta hai           |\n| Enumeration Tools  | `enum4linux`, `rpcclient`, `netexec`, `nmap`, `BloodHound` |\n| Enumeration Target | Users, Groups, Domain, Computers, Password Policy          |\n","x":1800,"y":1985,"width":582,"height":283},
		{"id":"6c168f3f53a4764c","type":"text","text":"`netexec smb <IP>`","x":1006,"y":2340,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6b34e9380e8e6901","type":"text","text":"`rpcclient -U \"\" <IP>`","x":742,"y":2340,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"15b7ffae401f1ac6","type":"text","text":"`enumdomgroups`","x":742,"y":2417,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4e938539f012da2d","type":"text","text":"`enumdomusers`","x":1006,"y":2417,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"54862e7a07a3976d","type":"text","text":"`enum4linux <IP>`","x":1103,"y":2497,"width":153,"height":60},
		{"id":"7065128b480da1c0","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script smb-enum-users -p445 <IP>`","x":740,"y":2497,"width":343,"height":60},
		{"id":"2971751f0822ff45","type":"text","text":"#### DNS Zone Transfer","x":484,"y":2911,"width":201,"height":60},
		{"id":"62e0f87fb0ef6309","type":"text","text":"DNS Zone Transfer ek process hai jisme ek DNS Server apni DNS zone ki complete information dusre DNS Server ko copy/share karta hai.\n\nSimple words me:\n\n```\nDNS Zone Transfer = Ek DNS server se dusre DNS server ko DNS records ki copy transfer karna.\n```","x":780,"y":2832,"width":560,"height":218},
		{"id":"db8a40c664eb05e6","type":"text","text":"DNS ka kaam hota hai:\n\n```\nDomain Name  --->  IP Address\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```\ngoogle.com  --->  142.250.x.x\n```\n\nYe information DNS Zone file me stored hoti hai.","x":1460,"y":2800,"width":390,"height":282},
		{"id":"064e4653ccd2ffd4","type":"text","text":"example.com\n\nA Record:\nwww.example.com     192.168.1.10\n\nMX Record:\nmail.example.com    192.168.1.20\n\nNS Record:\nns1.example.com\n\nTXT Record:\nSPF information","x":1460,"y":3280,"width":390,"height":346},
		{"id":"7cc62d0f6a6cbc32","type":"text","text":"# Zone Transfer ki zarurat kyu hoti hai?\n\nEk company ke paas usually multiple DNS servers hote hain.","x":2000,"y":2858,"width":482,"height":83},
		{"id":"10dd08c77baa2cf1","type":"text","text":"              Primary DNS\n              (Master)\n                  |\n                  |\n            Zone Transfer\n                  |\n                  v\n              Secondary DNS\n              (Slave)\n\nAgar Primary DNS fail ho jaye to Secondary DNS requests handle kar sake.","x":2087,"y":3000,"width":309,"height":382},
		{"id":"b034f34c35f991d1","type":"text","text":"Types of Zone Transfer","x":2116,"y":2740,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d7e58268434e6fd1","type":"text","text":"AXFR (Full Zone Transfer)","x":1962,"y":2536,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"26b5f77d148c64ed","type":"text","text":"IXFR (Incremental Zone Transfer)","x":2254,"y":2536,"width":285,"height":60},
		{"id":"94b169f45648b822","type":"text","text":"keval changed zone copy hota h","x":2257,"y":2463,"width":282,"height":60},
		{"id":"e7d8585ecc0d0c15","type":"text","text":"full zone copy hota h","x":1962,"y":2463,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"100fd7e6ec36fb2a","type":"text","text":"|Protocol|Port|\n|---|---|\n|DNS|TCP/UDP 53|\n|Zone Transfer|TCP 53|","x":2539,"y":2720,"width":258,"height":100},
		{"id":"dfba9cae99eaf2c8","type":"text","text":"Agar DNS server galat configure hai aur koi bhi zone transfer kar sakta hai, to attacker puri DNS information nikal sakta hai.\n\nInformation mil sakti hai:\n\n```\nSubdomains\nHostnames\nIP addresses\nMail servers\nInternal servers\nNetwork structure\n```","x":2840,"y":2463,"width":490,"height":306},
		{"id":"92650e58b4e7557b","type":"text","text":"`server ns1.example.com\nls domain.com`","x":2539,"y":2840,"width":319,"height":60},
		{"id":"56a95194f8ee7f8b","type":"text","text":"`host -l domain.com ns1.example.com`","x":2539,"y":2911,"width":319,"height":60},
		{"id":"07903b67b55c0ccd","type":"text","text":"`dig axfr example.com @ns1.example.com`","x":2539,"y":2990,"width":327,"height":60},
		{"id":"4169273b272bc974","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script dns-zone-transfer -p53 <DNS-IP>`","x":2540,"y":3060,"width":391,"height":60},
		{"id":"c8ee869959ef49c2","type":"text","text":"`dig axfr domain.com @dns-server`","x":2866,"y":2840,"width":280,"height":60},
		{"id":"effe5aff9580bccd","type":"text","text":"`nslookup`","x":2866,"y":2911,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a79acacc28a6ce8a","type":"text","text":"#### LDAP Enumeration","x":380,"y":4280,"width":232,"height":60},
		{"id":"dff8c77cc5359f7b","type":"text","text":"LDAP Enumeration ka matlab hai LDAP server se information collect karna jaise users, groups, domain details, computers aur organization structure.\n\nSimple words me:\n\n```\nLDAP = Directory database ko access karne ka protocol\nLDAP Enumeration = Is database se useful information nikalna\n```","x":740,"y":4189,"width":553,"height":242},
		{"id":"871ab2b811afe5bd","type":"text","text":"###### LDAP Kya Hai?\n\n```\nLDAP ek protocol hai jo directory services ke saath communicate karta hai.\n```\n\nExample:\n\nMicrosoft Active Directory LDAP ka use karta hai.\nCompany ke users, groups aur computers ki information LDAP directory me hoti hai.","x":1440,"y":4189,"width":686,"height":242},
		{"id":"0d8a13eb72b0837b","type":"text","text":"| Port    | Protocol | Use                        |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------- |\n| TCP 389 | LDAP     | Normal LDAP communication  |\n| TCP 636 | LDAPS    | LDAP over SSL/TLS (Secure) |\n","x":1440,"y":4000,"width":423,"height":100},
		{"id":"ae4a875b95b8e1f7","type":"text","text":"###### LDAP Enumeration se kya mil sakta hai?\nAttacker/Admin find kar sakta hai:\n\nUsers\nGroups\nEmail addresses\nDomain name\nOrganizational Units (OU)\nComputer accounts\nPassword policies\nUser descriptions","x":2260,"y":4157,"width":335,"height":306},
		{"id":"21d16b070074b7ff","type":"text","text":"| Term                     | Meaning                 |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------- |\n| DN (Distinguished Name)  | Object ka complete path |\n| CN (Common Name)         | Object ka naam          |\n| DC (Domain Component)    | Domain ka part          |\n| OU (Organizational Unit) | Objects ka container    |\n","x":2720,"y":4157,"width":421,"height":169},
		{"id":"2b39c60b63960337","type":"text","text":"`CN=Akash,OU=Users,DC=example,DC=com`","x":2720,"y":4360,"width":421,"height":60},
		{"id":"92aee3352460e9bb","type":"text","text":"`ldapsearch -x -H ldap://<IP> -b \"dc=example,dc=com\"`","x":740,"y":4100,"width":438,"height":60},
		{"id":"0887496889991eea","type":"text","text":"`ldapsearch -x -H ldap://192.168.1.10`","x":740,"y":4020,"width":319,"height":60},
		{"id":"a3e59cea8bb9826c","type":"text","text":"`ldapsearch -x -h <IP>`","x":740,"y":3940,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"03b2c3e5e74620f2","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script ldap* -p389 <IP>`","x":1080,"y":4020,"width":306,"height":60},
		{"id":"26bcb3a8b91e429d","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sV -p389 <IP>`","x":1201,"y":4100,"width":185,"height":60},
		{"id":"b030392ac174117b","type":"text","text":"`nmap -p389 <IP>`","x":1017,"y":3940,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"54eed306a99530da","type":"text","text":"| LDAP               | Active Directory        |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------- |\n| Protocol hai       | Directory service hai   |\n| Data access method | Data store + management |\n| Port 389/636       | LDAP ka use karta hai   |\n","x":1440,"y":4460,"width":398,"height":134},
		{"id":"76e0debdb13a6033","type":"text","text":"| Point            | Answer                                          |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Full Form        | Lightweight Directory Access Protocol           |\n| Purpose          | Directory information access karna              |\n| Used With        | Active Directory                                |\n| Port             | TCP 389                                         |\n| Secure Port      | TCP 636                                         |\n| Data             | Users, Groups, Computers, OUs                   |\n| Tool             | `ldapsearch`, `nmap`                            |\n| Enumeration Goal | AD structure aur user information collect karna |\n","x":3300,"y":4157,"width":526,"height":283},
		{"id":"92b86dc6624b7b24","type":"text","text":"# NFS","x":896,"y":5289,"width":79,"height":60},
		{"id":"018ce11a302e3479","type":"text","text":"**NFS** ek protocol hai jo network par **files aur directories share** karne ke liye use hota hai.\n\nSimple words:\n\n> **NFS = Linux/Unix systems me network ke through folder sharing.**","x":1100,"y":5215,"width":360,"height":209},
		{"id":"e9122cd59eb18a6f","type":"text","text":"Client remote folder ko apne system me mount kar sakta hai.","x":1100,"y":5080,"width":360,"height":60},
		{"id":"e438b670b20a695b","type":"text","text":"| Port         | Service        |\n| ------------ | -------------- |\n| TCP/UDP 2049 | NFS            |\n| TCP/UDP 111  | RPC Portmapper |\n","x":1132,"y":4920,"width":296,"height":100},
		{"id":"bd116026e572380b","type":"text","text":"##### NFS Enumeration se kya milta hai?\nAttacker discover kar sakta hai:\n\nShared directories\nAllowed clients\nExported folders\nPermissions\nRead/Write access","x":1620,"y":5202,"width":310,"height":236},
		{"id":"6191fb0e9d62d926","type":"text","text":"#### NFS Export File\nServer par:\n`/etc/exports`\n\nExample:\n`/home/share 192.168.1.0/24(rw)`\n\nMeaning:\n```\n/home/share → shared folder\n192.168.1.0/24 → allowed network\nrw → read/write permission\n```","x":2080,"y":5146,"width":332,"height":349},
		{"id":"2403e6569fd231c3","type":"text","text":"`nmap -p111,2049 <IP>`","x":1620,"y":4980,"width":193,"height":60},
		{"id":"1baf15ec7fe9923e","type":"text","text":"`showmount -e 192.168.1.10`","x":1827,"y":4980,"width":232,"height":60},
		{"id":"982162719557e330","type":"text","text":"`mount -t nfs 192.168.1.10:/home/share /mnt`","x":1620,"y":4910,"width":439,"height":60},
		{"id":"c41ae6097404ab96","type":"text","text":"`mount -t nfs <IP>:/share /mnt`","x":1620,"y":5050,"width":264,"height":60},
		{"id":"be5c6f713ae231a7","type":"text","text":"`showmount -e <IP>`","x":1890,"y":5050,"width":169,"height":60},
		{"id":"9a29589a0ded5bb8","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script nfs* -p111,2049 <IP>`","x":1620,"y":5126,"width":439,"height":60},
		{"id":"e44abd83c630d3d7","type":"text","text":"### RPC (Remote Procedure Call)","x":896,"y":5860,"width":317,"height":59},
		{"id":"bc2a10d69ca4bd73","type":"text","text":"**RPC (Remote Procedure Call)** ek protocol/mechanism hai jo ek computer ko **dusre computer par koi function ya service remotely execute** karne deta hai, bina ye soche ki service local hai ya remote.\n\n👉 Simple words:\n\n> **RPC = Dusre computer ko bolna: \"Mere liye ye kaam kar do.\"**","x":1367,"y":5790,"width":563,"height":199},
		{"id":"2ff208087ea494a8","type":"text","text":"          RPC Request\n Client -----------------> Server\n        \"Open File\"\n\n Client <----------------- Server\n         File Content","x":2040,"y":5781,"width":277,"height":218},
		{"id":"34157e37f9b481af","type":"text","text":"##### RPC Port Mapper\n\nRPC services alag-alag ports par chal sakti hain.\nIsliye Port Mapper ka use hota hai.\n\nPort Mapper ka kaam:\n\n```\nKaunsi RPC service kis port par chal rahi hai batana.\n```\n\nPort:\n\n```\nTCP/UDP 111\n```","x":2480,"y":5716,"width":498,"height":348},
		{"id":"e435a1af78f3263c","type":"text","text":"                Client\n                   |\n                   |\n           Port Mapper (111)\n                   |\n      --------------------------\n      |            |           |\n     NFS         Mountd      Other\n    2049         20048       30000","x":2571,"y":5321,"width":316,"height":282},
		{"id":"15874d76f8abeeaf","type":"text","text":"##### RPC Services\n```\nRPC khud ek service nahi hai.\nYe dusri services ko access karne ka framework hai.\n```\n\nExamples:\n\nNFS\nMountd\nNIS\nStatus Monitor","x":3120,"y":5724,"width":308,"height":332},
		{"id":"410f1eb40ba90ed0","type":"text","text":"##### Agar Port 111 open ho,\n\nAttacker ye dekh sakta hai:\n```\nKaunsi RPC services chal rahi hain\nUnke ports\nNFS available hai ya nahi\nMount services\nBackup services\n```","x":2978,"y":5328,"width":348,"height":268},
		{"id":"3a636f4e5d1c83cb","type":"text","text":"`nmap --script rpcinfo -p111 <IP>`","x":3563,"y":5996,"width":297,"height":60},
		{"id":"9dd1472b60e0c983","type":"text","text":"`rpcinfo -p <IP>`","x":3563,"y":5920,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"52ea484dfc36897e","type":"text","text":"`nmap -sV -p111 <IP>`","x":3563,"y":5830,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3ebd0465e6a8e217","type":"text","text":"`nmap -p111 <IP>`","x":3563,"y":5740,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1db1feb2d281eac5","type":"text","text":"Attacker\n     |\n     | rpcinfo -p\n     |\n     v\nPort 111\n     |\n     |\n     +------> NFS (2049)\n     |\n     +------> mountd (20048)\n     |\n     +------> statusd","x":4020,"y":5724,"width":233,"height":346},
		{"id":"e8bb287377f59b24","type":"text","text":"| RPC                                 | NFS                      |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| Remote procedure call mechanism     | File sharing protocol    |\n| Port 111                            | Port 2049                |\n| Service ka location batata hai      | Files share karta hai    |\n| Multiple services support karta hai | RPC par depend karta hai |\n","x":4340,"y":5724,"width":495,"height":169},
		{"id":"c45b7651ce85494d","type":"text","text":"| Point            | Answer                                                    |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Full Form        | Remote Procedure Call                                     |\n| Purpose          | Remote system par function/service execute karna          |\n| Port Mapper      | TCP/UDP 111                                               |\n| Used By          | NFS, Mountd, NIS, etc.                                    |\n| Enumeration Tool | `rpcinfo`, `nmap`                                         |\n| Risk             | Running RPC services aur unke ports ka pata chal jata hai |\n","x":4340,"y":5920,"width":600,"height":228},
		{"id":"a4b209366e47bbd1","type":"text","text":"BGP (Border Gateway Protocol) internet ka routing protocol hai jo alag-alag networks (Autonomous Systems - AS) ke beech best route choose karta hai.\n\n👉 Simple words:\n\n> BGP internet ka GPS hai. Ye batata hai ki data ko ek network se dusre network tak kis route se jana chahiye.","x":1032,"y":6660,"width":499,"height":254},
		{"id":"e1f8aa96bddc5051","type":"text","text":"BGP","x":820,"y":6757,"width":63,"height":60},
		{"id":"61cf50ce6fb9aba4","type":"text","text":"Maan lo tum Jio network par ho aur Google ki website open karte ho.\n\nData ka path kuch aisa ho sakta hai:\n\nYour PC\n    |\n    |\nJio Network (AS55836)\n    |\n    |\nInternet\n    |\n    |\nGoogle Network (AS15169)\n\nYe decide kaun karta hai ki packet kis-kis network se hokar Google tak pahunchhe?\n ","x":936,"y":6160,"width":692,"height":394},
		{"id":"13a0cd3377793699","type":"text","text":"Ek **Autonomous System (AS)** ek organization ya ISP ka network hota hai.\n\nHar AS ka ek unique number hota hai, jise **ASN (Autonomous System Number)** kehte hain.","x":1960,"y":6720,"width":382,"height":135},
		{"id":"1a82a83357cd1049","type":"text","text":"| Company    | ASN     |\n| ---------- | ------- |\n| Google     | AS15169 |\n| Cloudflare | AS13335 |\n| Jio        | AS55836 |\n","x":2037,"y":6440,"width":228,"height":134},
		{"id":"01822ecc3fd2a7c4","type":"text","text":"# BGP Kaise Kaam Karta Hai?\n\n### Step 1\n\nRouter apne neighbor se connection banata hai.\n\n↓\n\n### Step 2\n\nApne known routes share karta hai.\n\n↓\n\n### Step 3\n\nNeighbor apne routes share karta hai.\n\n↓\n\n### Step 4\n\nBGP best route select karta hai.","x":657,"y":7020,"width":389,"height":553},
		{"id":"b396400b7d1fa893","type":"text","text":"#### Cybersecurity me BGP\n\nAgar BGP misconfigure ho jaye to:\n```\nTraffic galat route par ja sakta hai.\nTraffic intercept ho sakta hai.\nInternet outage ho sakti hai.\n```","x":2580,"y":6677,"width":371,"height":221},
		{"id":"10d2dcd021be61b3","type":"text","text":"| BGP              | OSPF                         |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Internet routing | Internal network routing     |\n| Between AS       | Within one AS                |\n| TCP 179          | IP Protocol 89 (not TCP/UDP) |\n| Policy-based     | Link-state routing           |\n","x":1140,"y":7404,"width":386,"height":169},
		{"id":"df0bf49e6ecb47bf","type":"text","text":"| eBGP                  | iBGP             |\n| --------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Different AS ke beech | Same AS ke andar |\n| Internet routing      | Internal routing |\n","x":1140,"y":7280,"width":354,"height":100},
		{"id":"6dc7bb50c4016f9f","type":"text","text":"| Protocol | Port |\n| -------- | ---- |\n| TCP      | 179  |\n","x":1140,"y":7190,"width":177,"height":65},
		{"id":"fbfb03bdd2e11378","type":"text","text":"| Term          | Meaning                                      |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| AS            | Autonomous System                            |\n| ASN           | Autonomous System Number                     |\n| Peer/Neighbor | Do BGP routers jo routes exchange karte hain |\n| Route         | Network tak pahunchne ka path                |\n","x":1140,"y":7016,"width":494,"height":169},
		{"id":"174c339b3ef9f510","type":"text","text":"| Point     | Answer                                        |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Full Form | Border Gateway Protocol                       |\n| Purpose   | Different Autonomous Systems ke beech routing |\n| Port      | TCP 179                                       |\n| Used On   | Internet                                      |\n| AS        | Autonomous System                             |\n| ASN       | Autonomous System Number                      |\n| eBGP      | Different AS                                  |\n| iBGP      | Same AS                                       |\n| Risk      | BGP Hijacking, Route Manipulation             |\n","x":1540,"y":7200,"width":477,"height":310},
		{"id":"fa09787456519be5","type":"text","text":"#### OS Fingerprinting","x":100,"y":8417,"width":189,"height":60},
		{"id":"bff863c0cb1e1fad","type":"text","text":"OS Fingerprinting ka matlab hai target machine ka Operating System (Windows, Linux, macOS, etc.) identify karna bina us machine par login kiye.\n\n👉 Simple words:\n\n> OS Fingerprinting = Target ka Operating System pata lagana.","x":383,"y":8360,"width":603,"height":175},
		{"id":"3f6da8fc03ed56e9","type":"text","text":" Tumhe ek IP mila:\n\n```\n192.168.1.10\n```\n\nTumhe nahi pata ki ye:\n\n```\nWindows hai?\nUbuntu hai?\nKali hai?\nWindows Server hai?\n```\n\nOS Fingerprinting se ye pata lagaya ja sakta hai.","x":490,"y":7920,"width":390,"height":354},
		{"id":"45dbd8de5a52f5bf","type":"text","text":"##### OS Fingerprinting kaise kaam karta hai?\n`Har Operating System network packets ka response thoda alag deta hai.\n`\nExample:\n\n```\nTCP Window Size\nTTL (Time To Live)\nTCP Flags\nICMP Response\nTCP Options\n```\n\nScanner in responses ko analyze karta hai aur OS ka guess karta hai.","x":1120,"y":8282,"width":583,"height":332},
		{"id":"e6e8494c73ffddf8","type":"text","text":"          Attacker\n              |\n     TCP/ICMP Probes\n              |\n              v\n        Target Machine\n              |\n     Different Responses\n              |\n              v\n      \"Windows 10\"","x":1293,"y":7880,"width":237,"height":330},
		{"id":"b3ff6e1a013c939a","type":"text","text":"Active OS Fingerprinting","x":1963,"y":8124,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9c6ea51912ba1b65","type":"text","text":"Scanner target ko packets bhejta hai aur response analyze karta hai.\n\n```\nScanner\n   |\nTCP/ICMP Packets\n   |\nTarget\n   |\nResponse\n   |\nOperating System Guess\n```\n\n### Tools\n\n- Nmap\n- Xprobe2","x":2360,"y":7941,"width":620,"height":426},
		{"id":"6ca815d99cd5c4f8","type":"text","text":"Passive OS Fingerprinting","x":1968,"y":8634,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e98a040bfe39013e","type":"text","text":"Target ko koi packet nahi bheja jata.\n\nSirf existing network traffic observe kiya jata hai.\n\n```\nNetwork Traffic\n        |\n        |\n Passive Analyzer\n        |\n        |\n    Linux\n```\nTools\n- p0f\n- Wireshark (analysis)\n\nPassive fingerprinting stealthy hoti hai kyunki target ko probe nahi bheja jata.","x":2360,"y":8433,"width":620,"height":463},
		{"id":"b47707aae51f5621","type":"text","text":"`nmap -O <IP>`","x":3020,"y":7941,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ee7bd8c8ba776510","type":"text","text":"`nmap -O 192.168.1.10`","x":3020,"y":8020,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ba24bb0aadb83d6f","type":"text","text":"| Active              | Passive                         |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| Packets bhejte hain | Sirf traffic observe karte hain |\n| Faster              | Stealthy                        |\n| Detect ho sakta hai | Detect hona mushkil             |\n| Example: Nmap       | Example: p0f                    |\n","x":3300,"y":8300,"width":413,"height":169},
		{"id":"74a4dbf45a1a891a","type":"text","text":"`nmap -O <IP>`","x":3300,"y":8500,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ae66e8bd07da285f","type":"text","text":"``nmap -A <IP>``","x":3300,"y":8580,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4a3603208aee34da","x":3626,"y":8513,"width":175,"height":194,"type":"text","text":"Ye detect karta hai:\n\nOS\nVersion\nServices\nTraceroute\nNSE Scripts"},
		{"id":"609ea0ba471a8f8e","x":3300,"y":8647,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"`nmap -sV <IP>`"},
		{"id":"7675e311bd957b07","x":3300,"y":8740,"width":353,"height":226,"type":"text","text":"OS Fingerprinting me kya identify hota hai?\n```\n`Operating System\nOS Version\nDevice Type\nArchitecture\nNetwork Stack`\n```"},
		{"id":"58da022992e4aa9d","x":3740,"y":8220,"width":532,"height":283,"type":"text","text":"| Point                | Answer                                    |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| OS Fingerprinting    | Target ka Operating System identify karna |\n| Active               | Packets bhejkar detection                 |\n| Passive              | Traffic observe karke detection           |\n| Active Tool          | `nmap -O`                                 |\n| Passive Tool         | `p0f`                                     |\n| Nmap Aggressive Scan | `nmap -A <IP>`                            |\n| Detects              | OS, Version, Device Type                  |\n| `-A`                 | OS + Services + Version + Traceroute      |\n"}
	],
